Synthetic speech probe saying "test", generated for Spunto with eSpeak NG's
built-in en-us formant voice. No human recording, MBROLA voice, downloaded model
or operating-system voice is used.

Generator: eSpeak NG 1.52.0 (Debian package 1.52.0+dfsg-5).
Source and generator license: https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng (GPL-3.0-or-later).
The utterance and generated probe are distributed under Spunto's project license.

Generation commands (eSpeak NG and FFmpeg are development tools, not runtime
dependencies):

  espeak-ng -v en-us -s 175 -z -w health-source.wav "test"
  ffmpeg -i health-source.wav -ac 1 -ar 16000 -c:a pcm_s16le -map_metadata -1 \
    -fflags +bitexact -flags:a +bitexact health.wav

The result is non-silent, mono, 16-bit PCM at 16 kHz, shorter than the health
probe's one-second accounting limit. Generator/resampler versions may change
the waveform; the checked-in file is the runtime input.
